  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Delhi Police files multiple FIRs over CJP's 'Lehra Do Tiranga' protest",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/delhi-police-files-multiple-firs-over-cjp-s-lehra-do-tiranga-protest-126101700322_1.html",
      "description": "Delhi Police has registered multiple FIRs in connection with alleged violation of prohibitory orders in Connaught Place ahead of the Cockroach Janta Party's 'Lehra do Tiranga' protest a day ago, sources said on Saturday.\n\"Despite repeated announcements asking people to disperse, a crowd gathered in and around Connaught Place on Friday, prompting the police to initiate legal action,\" said the source.\nThe prohibitory orders, issued under Section 163 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, banned mass gatherings in Connaught Place and adjoining areas.\nHundreds of CJP supporters and student activists staged a series of flash protests across Connaught Place amid a massive police deployment on Friday, demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-17T06:41:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "Neha Bora released, Dipke to be produced before SEM court: Delhi Police",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/neha-bora-released-dipke-to-be-produced-before-sem-court-delhi-police-126101700085_1.html",
      "description": "All India Students' Association (AISA) president Neha Bora was released early Saturday morning, while Cockroach Janata Party (CJP) founder Abhijeet Dipke will be produced before the SEM court, Delhi Police said.\nBoth were taken into preventive custody ahead of the 'Lehra Do Tiranga' protest march at Connaught Place here on Friday.\nBora was released after completing formalities related to her detention under Section 65 of the Delhi Police Act, while action was initiated against Dipke under Sections 126 and 170 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS), police said.\nDipke was subsequently arrested and will be produced before the Special Executive Magistrate (SEM) court later in the day, police sources said.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-17T02:08:40"
    }
  ]
